`backend = age` with `signer = gpg` is refused when the config loads, and `seal`, `unseal` and `check` refuse it on a config built in code. gpg signs only what it encrypts, so that pair signed and verified nothing: changing one config line let an unsigned record, built from the public recipient alone, through a plain `unseal`. An unknown `backend` or `signer` value is refused too, instead of falling back to gpg or skipping the check under `--allow-unsigned`.
